"""site/build-site --commit COMMIT --sha256 DIR [--out DIR]: the project's
web page, one static HTML page and its stylesheet, made from README.md and
the machine's docs page (docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst, as patches/
leave it), so that it says what they say.

Its downloads are COMMIT's builds on the `prebuilt` release, one for each
platform in the README's table of prebuilt binaries, with the SHA-256s in
DIR's qemu-chumby-COMMIT-PLATFORM.tar.xz.sha256 (CI's build artifacts; the
tarballs beside them, if there, give their sizes). It writes OUT (default
_site): index.html, style.css and downloads.json, the downloads as
[{platform, name, url, sha256, sha256_url, size}].

Python 3's standard library only. The README and the docs page are read
with small parsers for the Markdown and reStructuredText they use, which
refuse anything else, so that a construct they don't know fails the build
rather than showing up mangled.
"""
